Yes, that's "as expected", except I usually go
through with a hand edit and knock the quote marks
off the blank lines, which makes the result a bit
prettier and also, since my sites implement quoted
versus original line-count rules, helps by scoring
the blank lines as original instead of quoted.

Hand editing, because my editing tool, vim() is
smart about news/email quoting conventions, also
lets me reflow quoted material narrower so that
buggy posting sites don't wrap it unexpectedly,
leaving the mess we all recognized as occurring
much too often.

